1. DEFINITIONS

"FanXora" means FanXora Innovation & Technology Group L.L.C.

"Operator" means FanXor Dynamics LLC, which operates StoneAI under FanXora's
authorization and applicable operating terms, policies, and controls.

"Software" means the StoneAI CLI executable, installers, updates, documentation,
configuration files, and accompanying materials distributed by or on behalf of
FanXora.

"Service" means the proprietary StoneAI cloud platform and associated backend,
governance, orchestration, security, compliance, routing, and audit infrastructure.

"User" means any individual or entity authorized to install, access, or use the
Software or Service.

2. OWNERSHIP

As between FanXora and the User, the Software, Service, source code, object code,
architecture, algorithms, documentation, user interfaces, designs, models, prompts,
workflows, databases, trade secrets, trademarks, copyrights, patents, know-how, and
other proprietary rights embodied in or associated with StoneAI are proprietary to
FanXora or its applicable licensors.

Nothing in this Agreement transfers ownership to the User. No ownership right arises
by implication, estoppel, access, possession, disclosure, or continued use.

3. OPERATING AND DISTRIBUTION STRUCTURE

FanXor Dynamics LLC operates StoneAI on behalf of FanXora under authorization.
FanXus Omnivations L.L.C. may act as an authorized reseller or distributor where
expressly authorized by FanXora.

No operator, reseller, distributor, customer, contractor, or User receives ownership
of StoneAI intellectual property merely by performing an authorized role.

4. LIMITED LICENSE

Subject to this Agreement and any applicable subscription, order form, master
agreement, acceptable-use policy, or customer agreement, FanXora grants the User a
limited, revocable, non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable right to:

  * install authorized copies of the Software;
  * execute authorized, unmodified copies of the Software; and
  * access the Service solely for authorized business purposes.

No other rights are granted.

5. NO IMPLIED LICENSES

No license or right is granted except as expressly stated in an applicable written
agreement. All rights not expressly granted are reserved.

6. PROHIBITED ACTIVITIES

Except to the extent a restriction is expressly prohibited by applicable law, the User
shall not:

  * modify, reproduce, redistribute, sublicense, sell, rent, lease, or host the
    Software except as expressly authorized;
  * create unauthorized derivative works;
  * reverse engineer, decompile, disassemble, decode, or reconstruct source code;
  * bypass authentication, authorization, subscription, metering, rate-limiting,
    licensing, safety, or technical protection controls;
  * extract proprietary models, prompts, system instructions, confidential data, or
    trade secrets;
  * scrape or reproduce proprietary data or protected workflows outside authorized
    interfaces;
  * use prompt injection, exfiltration techniques, or other circumvention methods to
    obtain protected system information;
  * remove or alter proprietary, copyright, trademark, security, or licensing notices;
  * share credentials or permit unauthorized access;
  * benchmark the Service for public competitive publication without written
    authorization where such restriction is enforceable; or
  * use the Software or Service in violation of applicable law or governing agreements.

7. SERVICE ACCESS AND SECURITY

Access may require authentication, subscription, payment, device authorization,
licensing verification, compliance checks, security controls, and usage limitations.
FanXora or the Operator may suspend, limit, revoke, or terminate access where
reasonably necessary to address security risks, misuse, non-payment, legal obligations,
credential compromise, material breach, or other grounds permitted by applicable
agreements and law.

8. ACCEPTABLE USE AND GOVERNING POLICIES

The then-current StoneAI Acceptable Use Policy, privacy notices, security requirements,
and other policies expressly incorporated into an applicable agreement form part of
the User's authorized-use conditions. Material changes requiring renewed assent will
be presented through an appropriate notice or acceptance process where required by
law or contract.

9. CREDENTIALS, ENTITLEMENTS, AND ACCOUNTS

API keys, activation codes, entitlements, subscriptions, and accounts are access
mechanisms, not transfers of ownership. Users must protect credentials and may not
sell, transfer, publish, or share them except where an applicable agreement expressly
permits delegated administration.

FanXora or the Operator may rotate, reset, suspend, or revoke credentials and
entitlements for security, legal, contractual, billing, or operational reasons.

10. INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY

Distribution of the CLI does not grant ownership of or a license to server-side
technology, governance logic, orchestration systems, prompts, model instructions,
APIs, databases, confidential information, trade secrets, or other proprietary
technology beyond the limited rights expressly granted for authorized use.

11. CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION

Users may receive access to confidential or proprietary information through the
Software or Service. Confidentiality obligations arise only to the extent provided by
an applicable agreement, accepted terms, confidentiality policy, nondisclosure
agreement, law, or other enforceable obligation. Nothing in this Agreement creates an
"implied NDA" solely from passive viewing or access.

Unauthorized disclosure or misuse of protected confidential information may give rise
to contractual, equitable, administrative, civil, or other remedies as permitted by
applicable law.

