26. SEVERABILITY

If any provision is held invalid or unenforceable, the remaining provisions remain in
effect to the extent permitted by law. An invalid provision will be limited or
modified only to the minimum extent necessary to preserve lawful effect.

27. WAIVER

Failure to enforce a provision on one occasion does not constitute a continuing waiver
of that provision or any other right.

28. ENTIRE AGREEMENT AND ORDER OF PRECEDENCE

This Agreement governs the CLI unless superseded or supplemented by an executed order
form, master agreement, enterprise agreement, reseller agreement, or other written
